2. The compiled agent — bundled third-party code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

scripts/frida/socket_trace.bundle.js is a build artifact produced by
frida-compile from agent/src/. It is not only our code: the build inlines its
dependencies, so the file shipped in this repository CONTAINS the packages below
and redistributes them.

    frida-java-bridge
    Copyright (C) Ole André Vadla Ravnås and contributors
    https://github.com/frida/frida-java-bridge
    Licensed under LGPL-2.0 WITH WxWindows-exception-3.1

    buffer            (C) Feross Aboukhadijeh and contributors — MIT
    base64-js         (C) Jameson Little — MIT
    ieee754           (C) Feross Aboukhadijeh and contributors — BSD-3-Clause
    https://github.com/feross/buffer, /beatgammit/base64-js, /feross/ieee754

frida-java-bridge supplies the Java runtime bridge. Frida 17 removed the built-in
`Java` global, so without this package there is no call-stack attribution at all;
it is a functional necessity, not a convenience. The wxWindows exception to
LGPL-2.0 permits distributing a combined work under the combined work's own terms
— here AGPL-3.0 — while the bridge's own portions remain under its licence, and
this notice is part of satisfying that. The MIT and BSD-3-Clause components are
redistributed with the attributions above.

To rebuild the artifact from source and confirm it contains nothing else:

    cd agent && npm ci && npm run build

The build is byte-for-byte reproducible; tests/test_bundle_fresh.py verifies that
the shipped bundle matches agent/src/.

